    "assistant_text": "Found the root cause: `settle()` computes the discount by rounding each line item individually and summing (932 + 3522 + 6112 = 10566 cents), but rounding the discount once on the subtotal gives 10567 cents \u2014 a one-cent difference from accumulated per-item rounding. The test expects the subtotal-based total (1324.83), so the fix is to discount the subtotal once instead of looping over line items.\nAll 6 tests pass now.\n\n**Root cause**: `settle()` in `src/ledger/engine.py` was computing the promotional discount per line item (rounding each to the nearest cent) and summing those, instead of rounding once on the subtotal. For this invoice (126.00 + 476.00 + 826.00), per-item rounding gave 105.66 in discount, while subtotal-based rounding gives 105.67 \u2014 the missing cent that made `total_due` come out to 1324.84 instead of 1324.83.\n\n**Fix**: replaced the per-item loop with a single `rules.discount_for(subtotal)` call, so the discount is rounded once against the subtotal \u2014 matching how `total_due` is expected to reconcile with an exact payment.",
